# Defect 547, 2026-10-10, panel 203's R2, ratified by the author with *close
# 547 on the measurement*: a self-call through a parameter. `step` hands
# itself to `go`, which calls what it is handed, so every call of `step`
# calls `step` again before it returns, and `check` does not refuse it: no
# rule follows a call through a parameter to what the callers hand it, and
# doing so was the summary route the sitting measured and did not take (205
# lines, +1.3% on every `check`, five shapes refused and three still missed,
# this file's two siblings among them). The answer is panel 199 R2's,
# at every level: the recursion runs until the stack is exhausted, an abort
# that says so, never a crash. Under the sanitiser the runtime's guard yields
# to ASan, which says `stack-overflow`.

function go(n: i64, f: (function(i64) -> i64)) -> i64
    return f(n)

function step(n: i64) -> i64
    return go(n: n, f: step)

function main()
    print(step(1))
